    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other two files are support classes).\n\n## What I changed\n\n`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the `audit` step of the `POST /api/owners` pipeline. It already wrote the human-readable audit line; I added, alongside it, an immutable structured event emitted through the same `AUDIT` logger:\n\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nKey points of the implementation:\n\n- **Immutable & structured** \u2014 the event is a `record OwnerCreatedEvent(seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event)`, serialized to a single JSON object via Jackson (`tools.jackson`, already the project's mapper). The record's component order fixes the JSON key order.\n- **Monotonic `seq`** \u2014 a process-wide `static AtomicLong` incremented once per create.\n- **Carries the current primary identifier** \u2014 the `customerCode` value comes from a `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper. This is the seam the spec calls out: when the customer code is later unified into a member id, that one method returns the member id and every emitted event follows automatically, with no other change to this class.\n- The original audit line is untouched, so both are written per the spec's \"in addition to the audit line\".\n\nThe acceptance test `coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` \u2014 which asserts one AUDIT message contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the read-back `customerCode` \u2014 now passes.",
